<div class="page-header">
  <h2>Institutions</h2>
  <a href="/institutions/new" class="btn btn-primary">+ Add</a>
</div>
<p class="page-desc">Your BD network — agencies, primes, foundations, and universities you want to work with or already do. Use relationship status to track where each org is in your pipeline.</p>

<details class="how-to">
  <summary>How to use Institutions</summary>
  <div class="how-to-body">
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Start with your target list, not just your history.</strong> Add every agency, funder, and prime contractor you want to pursue — even if you've never had a conversation with them. That's what <em>Target</em> status is for.</li>
      <li>Move orgs through the pipeline as the relationship develops: <strong>Target → Prospect</strong> (you've made contact) <strong>→ Partner</strong> (active teaming or collaboration) <strong>→ Client</strong> (they've awarded you work).</li>
      <li>Use <strong>Vendor</strong> for subconsultants and suppliers you bring in on your proposals.</li>
      <li>Link contacts to their institution so every person in your network is one click from their org's profile, awards history, and opportunities.</li>
      <li>Use <strong>Save as Teaming Partner</strong> on USASpending to quickly add primes that win contracts in your space — they're both competitors and future teaming partners.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The list is sorted by relationship depth: Clients and Partners appear first, Targets last — so your hottest relationships are always at the top.</p>
  </div>
</details>

<form class="filter-bar" method="GET" action="/institutions">
  <input type="text" name="q" value="<%= filters.q || '' %>" placeholder="Search name…" class="filter-input">
  <select name="status" class="filter-input filter-input--sm">
    <option value="">All Statuses</option>
    <% statuses.forEach(function(s) { %>
      <option value="<%= s %>" <%= filters.status === s ? 'selected' : '' %>><%= s %></option>
    <% }); %>
  </select>
  <input type="text" name="state" value="<%= filters.state || '' %>" placeholder="State (e.g. CA)" class="filter-input filter-input--sm">
  <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary">Filter</button>
  <a href="/institutions" class="btn-link">Clear</a>
</form>

<% if (institutions.length === 0) { %>
  <p class="empty-state">No institutions found. <a href="/institutions/new">Add your first target organization.</a></p>
<% } else { %>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Name</th><th>Status</th><th>Type</th><th>City</th><th>State</th><th>Website</th><th></th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% institutions.forEach(function(i) { %>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="/institutions/<%= i.id %>"><%= i.name %></a></td>
            <td><span class="inst-status inst-status--<%= (i.relationship_status || 'Target').toLowerCase() %>"><%= i.relationship_status || 'Target' %></span></td>
            <td><%= i.institution_type || '—' %></td>
            <td><%= i.city || '—' %></td>
            <td><%= i.state || '—' %></td>
            <td><% if (i.website) { %><a href="<%= i.website %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&#8599;</a><% } else { %>—<% } %></td>
            <td>
              <form action="/institutions/<%= i.id %>/delete" method="POST" onsubmit="return confirm('Delete this institution? This cannot be undone.')">
                <button type="submit" class="btn-link btn-link--danger">Delete</button>
              </form>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% } %>
